# Discovery safety v1.4 development log (DEVELOPMENT SEEDS ONLY; nothing here is held-out)

## A. Residual false endorsements of v1.3 (seeds of round 4, development data now)
Reproduced on unchanged v1.3 in tests/unit/test_discovery_safety_v14_reproduction.py (commits 6c0f698, 06bc7d6).
Root cause 1 (all four): a rival counted as closed because a passed registration of the answer SEPARATED the predictions, while the rival's own evaluator prediction passed the same runs:
  leakage.substrate-06 b24: cutback test, scatter.sidewall p=0.022 passes; rival chain.polarization_drift p=0.186 and 'no effect' p=0.186 pass too (separation 3.41).
  noise_glitch-06 b8: baseline test, claim laser_drift+gap_small p=0.013; simpler rival laser_drift p=0.48 passes.
  noise_only_null-04 b8: gap_array test, claim gap_large p=0.012; 'no effect' p=0.55 passes.
Root cause 2: grammar shapes ignored by the open-rival check:
  width_wide-03 b8 (aliased): thickness claimed; catalog rivals were legitimately refuted, but all 270 adequate grammar shapes (single causes, many two-channel compositions) predict a power-sweep/width-array response >=3 SD away; power_sweep and width_array never run.
  leakage.substrate-06: 648 adequate grammar shapes separated (e.g. on cutback).
Root cause 2b (found during development, base 8000000): geometry.gap_small-01 b12, 'no effect' SUPPORTED with kappa 1.3, 1.1, 2.7 (sigma 1): 'no effect' was held only against catalog classes at smallest declared effects; 543 adequate grammar shapes fitted >=3 SD from zero.

